# High-level term of the DLPNO-CCSD(T):r2SCAN-3c ONIOM-style energy correction
# (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8: K + HOO- -> KP). See ../r2scan3c/job.inp for the full
# composite-correction formula and the low-level term it pairs with.
#
# Level and basis follow the ORCA project's own worked example for accurate
# reaction/activation energies (ORCA 6.1 Tutorials, "Calculating accurate
# energy barriers": https://www.faccts.de/docs/orca/6.1/tutorials/react/actibar.html),
# which refines a cheap DFT-optimized geometry with a
# "!DLPNO-CCSD(T) DEF2-TZVPP DEF2-TZVPP/C" single point rather than trusting
# any DFT functional for the final barrier. That tutorial's own justification
# is quantitative, not just "more expensive is better": density functionals
# (including range-separated hybrids such as wB97X-D on def2-TZVP) carry an
# RMSE of roughly 5 kcal/mol (~20 kJ/mol) against CCSD(T)-quality barriers,
# which sits right at COMPUTATIONAL.md's C7 gate (+/-20 kJ/mol) and is far
# wider than C8's target window (a 4 kJ/mol-wide band on ΔG of perhydrate
# formation) -- so for this project a DFT single point cannot be trusted to
# discriminate the C8 branches on its own; DLPNO-CCSD(T) can.
#
# Run on the QM-region fragment only (job.xyz =
# ../../geometry_r2scan3c-xtb/ts/job.QMRegion.xyz, 11 atoms, net charge -1),
# not the full 147-atom embedded system -- DLPNO-CCSD(T) on the whole catalyst
# is not attempted; only the correction term is.
#
# CPCM(water), TightSCF: matching COMPUTATIONAL.md's existing convention for
# every other isolated-species task in the register, so this number sits on
# the same footing as the rest.
#
# nprocs 8, not the machine's full 32 logical threads: benchmarked in place on
# this exact job (2026-09-09, homelab, i9-14900K, 8 P-cores/16 E-cores, 125 GB
# RAM) -- 8 ranks: 43.5 s wall; 16 ranks: 51.5 s; 24 ranks: 50.8 s. More ranks
# is SLOWER here, not faster: past the 8 physical P-cores, ranks either land
# on SMT siblings sharing one P-core's FP/vector units or on the slower
# E-cores, and MPI syncs the whole run to the slowest rank. This is a property
# of the hybrid P/E chip, not of DLPNO-CCSD(T) -- an 11-atom fragment simply
# doesn't have enough work to hide that imbalance. maxcore 4000 MB is already
# generous: the run's own MDCI module peaked at 1178 MB/core, so 8x4000 MB
# (32 GB) leaves most of the 125 GB free for other jobs to run concurrently --
# that, not a bigger nprocs on one job, is how this machine's capacity
# actually gets used across the C7-C10 family.

! DLPNO-CCSD(T) def2-TZVPP def2-TZVPP/C CPCM(Water) TightSCF

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
